# Trivy findings on ArchiBrief's own infra/ that are accepted on purpose.
# CI fails on any other HIGH/CRITICAL finding (ADR-0048). Each entry says
# why; remove it when the reason stops being true.

# S3 buckets use SSE-S3 (AES256), not a customer-managed KMS key. The data
# is review artifacts and a static site; a CMK adds per-request KMS cost and
# key management for no change in who can read the objects.
AWS-0132

# The budget-alert SNS topic (modules/cost-controls) is unencrypted. AWS
# Budgets can't publish to a topic encrypted with the AWS-managed aws/sns
# key, and the topic only carries budget threshold alerts.
AWS-0095

# No AWS WAF on the CloudFront distribution yet. Planned with the public
# submission quotas (master list Phase 3, item 17, ADR-0046).
AWS-0011
